                            <!-- ============ FAQ GROUP: Safety & Is This Tour Right for Me? ============ -->
                            <h1>Safety &amp; Is This Tour Right for Me?</h1>

                            <!-- accordion item - Safety -->
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading-safety">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                        data-bs-target="#faq-collapse-safety" aria-expanded="false"
                                        aria-controls="faq-collapse-safety">
                                        How do you keep guests safe in the water?
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq-collapse-safety" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                    aria-labelledby="flush-heading-safety">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Every tour includes a safety briefing before entering the water, and experienced safety divers stay with guests throughout the swim. The team closely watches shark behavior, ocean conditions, and the group so guests can focus on enjoying the experience.</p>
                                        <p>These are wild animals in the open ocean, so the sharks are always treated with respect and safety comes first.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <!--// accordion item - Safety -->

                            <!-- accordion item - Nervous -->
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading-nervous">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                        data-bs-target="#faq-collapse-nervous" aria-expanded="false"
                                        aria-controls="faq-collapse-nervous">
                                        I’m excited about shark diving, but also a little nervous. Is that normal?
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq-collapse-nervous" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                    aria-labelledby="flush-heading-nervous">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Absolutely. For many guests, getting into the open ocean with sharks is well outside their normal comfort zone.</p>
                                        <p>The crew will explain what to expect before you enter the water and stay with you throughout the experience. You’re never expected to do more than you’re comfortable doing.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <!--// accordion item - Nervous -->

                            <!-- accordion item - Swimming ability -->
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading-swimming">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                        data-bs-target="#faq-collapse-swimming" aria-expanded="false"
                                        aria-controls="faq-collapse-swimming">
                                        Do I need to be a strong swimmer or have diving experience?
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq-collapse-swimming" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                    aria-labelledby="flush-heading-swimming">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>No previous diving experience is required. Most of the experience takes place snorkeling at the surface, and the crew will assist you throughout the dive.</p>
                                        <p>You should be comfortable floating and moving through the water, but you do not need to be an experienced swimmer, freediver, or scuba diver.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <!--// accordion item - Swimming ability -->

                            <!-- accordion item - Scuba -->
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading-scuba">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                        data-bs-target="#faq-collapse-scuba" aria-expanded="false"
                                        aria-controls="faq-collapse-scuba">
                                        Is this a scuba diving tour?
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq-collapse-scuba" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                    aria-labelledby="flush-heading-scuba">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>No. This is a snorkeling and freediving experience, not a scuba dive. No scuba certification is required, and snorkel equipment is provided.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <!--// accordion item - Scuba -->

                            <!-- accordion item - Requirements -->
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading-requirements">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                        data-bs-target="#faq-collapse-requirements" aria-expanded="false"
                                        aria-controls="faq-collapse-requirements">
                                        Are there any age, health, or experience requirements?
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq-collapse-requirements" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                    aria-labelledby="flush-heading-requirements">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>The minimum age is 5 years old with an adult, and no previous shark-diving or scuba experience is required.</p>
                                        <p>Guests with serious health conditions should consult their physician before participating, particularly if they have concerns about being in the open ocean or climbing on and off the boat.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <!--// accordion item - Requirements -->

                            <!-- accordion item - Seasickness -->
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading-seasickness">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                        data-bs-target="#faq-collapse-seasickness" aria-expanded="false"
                                        aria-controls="faq-collapse-seasickness">
                                        What if I get seasick?
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq-collapse-seasickness" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                    aria-labelledby="flush-heading-seasickness">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Seasickness can happen, especially for guests who are sensitive to boat motion, and being on a small boat in the open ocean can cause seasickness even for people who don’t normally think of themselves as prone to it.</p>
                                        <p>If you’re sensitive to motion or think there’s a chance you may get seasick, the best thing you can do is prepare ahead of time. Motion-sickness medications and other preventative strategies are generally most effective when used before symptoms begin, so it’s worth looking into your options before the day of your tour.</p>
                                        <p>Getting a good night’s sleep, staying hydrated, avoiding alcohol the night before, and eating appropriately before the trip can also help.</p>
                                        <p>It’s also a good idea to familiarize yourself with what to do if you start feeling seasick while you’re on the boat. A little preparation can make a big difference in how much you enjoy the experience.</p>
                                        <p><strong><a href="/landing-pages/oahu-shark-diving/managing-seasickness/">Read our complete guide to preventing and managing seasickness before your tour.</a></strong></p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <!--// accordion item - Seasickness -->


                            <!-- ============ FAQ GROUP: The Shark Diving Experience ============ -->
                            <h1>The Shark Diving Experience</h1>

                            <!-- accordion item - What makes us different -->
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading-different">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                        data-bs-target="#faq-collapse-different" aria-expanded="false"
                                        aria-controls="faq-collapse-different">
                                        What makes Hawaii Adventure Diving different from other shark diving tours?
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq-collapse-different" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                    aria-labelledby="flush-heading-different">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>The goal is a more personal and immersive shark-diving experience rather than simply watching sharks from a distance.</p>
                                        <p>Tours are limited to a maximum of six guests, and the team includes highly experienced shark divers, divemasters, freedivers, captains, marine professionals, and underwater photographers who spend significant time working with sharks in the open ocean.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <!--// accordion item - What makes us different -->

                            <!-- accordion item - How close -->
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading-how-close">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                        data-bs-target="#faq-collapse-how-close" aria-expanded="false"
                                        aria-controls="faq-collapse-how-close">
                                        How close do we get to the sharks?
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq-collapse-how-close" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                    aria-labelledby="flush-heading-how-close">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>There is no fixed distance because every encounter is different and the sharks choose how they move through the water.</p>
                                        <p>Sharks often come quite close. When conditions and shark behavior allow, the team gives guests the freedom to have a more immersive encounter rather than simply observing from one position. If you would rather keep more distance, that is completely fine too.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <!--// accordion item - How close -->

                            <!-- accordion item - Shark species -->
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading-shark-species">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                        data-bs-target="#faq-collapse-shark-species" aria-expanded="false"
                                        aria-controls="faq-collapse-shark-species">
                                        What kinds of sharks are there?
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq-collapse-shark-species" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                    aria-labelledby="flush-heading-shark-species">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Common encounters can include Galapagos sharks, tiger sharks, hammerheads, and other pelagic shark species found around Oʻahu.</p>
                                        <p>The exact animals you encounter vary because these are wild sharks in their natural environment.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <!--// accordion item - Shark species -->

                            <!-- accordion item - Will I see sharks? -->
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading-see-sharks">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                        data-bs-target="#faq-collapse-see-sharks" aria-expanded="false"
                                        aria-controls="faq-collapse-see-sharks">
                                        Will I definitely see sharks?
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq-collapse-see-sharks" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                    aria-labelledby="flush-heading-see-sharks">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Sharks are wild animals, so wildlife encounters can never be guaranteed.</p>
                                        <p>Every day in the ocean is different, and shark activity can vary with conditions. That unpredictability is also part of what makes seeing them in their natural environment so special.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <!--// accordion item - Will I see sharks? -->

                            <!-- accordion item - Typical tour -->
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading-typical-tour">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                        data-bs-target="#faq-collapse-typical-tour" aria-expanded="false"
                                        aria-controls="faq-collapse-typical-tour">
                                        What happens on a typical tour?
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq-collapse-typical-tour" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                    aria-labelledby="flush-heading-typical-tour">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Your tour begins at Haleʻiwa Harbor, where you’ll meet the crew and get settled on the boat. Plan to arrive at least 15 minutes before your scheduled departure so there’s plenty of time to check in and get ready.</p>
                                        <p>From the harbor, it’s roughly a 15–30 minute boat ride to the shark diving site, about three miles offshore. Along the way, you’ll get great views of Oʻahu’s North Shore and may spot wildlife such as sea turtles, dolphins, flying fish, or even surfers near the harbor depending on the season and conditions.</p>
                                        <p>During the ride out, your safety diver will go over what to expect in the water, explain the equipment and safety procedures, talk about the sharks and surrounding marine environment, and answer any questions you have. It’s also a chance to get to know the crew and, if you’ve booked the photo package, your photographer.</p>
                                        <p>When you reach the dive site, a safety diver enters the water first to evaluate the conditions and shark activity. Once everything looks good, you’ll put on your snorkel gear and enter the water with the crew.</p>
                                        <p>Most guests spend around 45 minutes in the water, although the exact amount of dive time can vary with conditions. You’ll be able to snorkel at the surface, watch the sharks move through the water, and simply take in the experience. Guests who have booked photography can also work with the photographer on positioning, hand signals, and the kinds of shots they’d like to capture.</p>
                                        <p>If you want to take a break, you can return to the boat and get back in the water afterward, as conditions and timing allow.</p>
                                        <p>When the dive is finished, you’ll climb back aboard, dry off, change if you’d like, and get settled for the ride back to Haleʻiwa Harbor. The return trip is another chance to enjoy the North Shore from offshore and talk with the crew about the dive.</p>
                                        <p>Once back at the harbor, you’ll gather your belongings and head out from there. The full experience is usually just under two hours from departure to return.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <!--// accordion item - Typical tour -->

                            <!-- accordion item - Bathroom -->
